From 1828a19a002ce1a56fe71abad44cd8ef10956a1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hocking Lee <hockinglee@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 10:54:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add BLE serial mode (--ble)

Talk to a Bluetooth Low Energy device through a pair of GATT
characteristics, one written to and one notifying, like the ble-serial
project does (e.g. the Nordic UART Service).

  minicom --ble                 scan, pick a device and characteristics
  minicom --ble=AA:BB:..        connect directly
  --ble-adapter=hciN|ADDR       adapter to use
  --ble-write=UUID / --ble-read=UUID   characteristics to preselect

BlueZ is driven over D-Bus with sd-bus (libsystemd). The device list
and the characteristic dialog use minicom's own window library. The
NUS characteristics 6e400002-... (write) and 6e400003-... (read) are
preselected when present, so Enter on "Connect" is enough.

A detached helper process relays between a pty and the device, and
minicom opens the pty like a serial port, so capture, transfers and
scripts keep working. The helper:
 - writes in ATT MTU sized chunks, without response when allowed;
 - reconnects by itself when the link drops, the peer's GATT database
   changes, the device object expires, bluetoothd restarts or the
   adapter is re-enumerated (found again by its address);
 - discards data typed while the link is down instead of blocking;
 - exits and disconnects when minicom goes away (lifeline pipe EOF),
   also if minicom is killed.
Minicom shows a window while the link is down, and leaves with a
message (disconnecting the device) if the helper dies.

Setup errors (no bluetoothd, no adapter, rfkill, connect/service
discovery timeout, no suitable characteristics, StartNotify refused)
are reported in a window or on exit.

BLE support is built when libsystemd is found (--enable-ble, default
auto). MINICOM_BLE_LOG=<file> logs the helper's activity.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
