diff --git a/man/minicom.1 b/man/minicom.1
index 6b3d42f..8708df4 100644
--- a/man/minicom.1
+++ b/man/minicom.1
@@ -130,6 +130,44 @@ Buffering mode of capture file. MODE can be one of:
    L  Line buffered.
    F  Fully buffered.
 .TP 0.5i
+.B \-\-ble[=ADDRESS]
+BLE serial mode (only if minicom was built with BLE support): talk to a
+Bluetooth Low Energy device through a pair of GATT characteristics, one
+that is written to and one that sends notifications, in the same way as
+the ble-serial project. BlueZ (bluetoothd) must be running.
+.RS
+.PP
+Without ADDRESS, a list of the devices found by scanning is shown; pick
+one with the cursor keys and Enter. Press A to also show devices without
+a name. After connecting, the write and read characteristics are chosen
+in a dialog. The Nordic UART Service characteristics
+6e400002-b5a3-f393-e0a9-e50e24dcca9e (write) and
+6e400003-b5a3-f393-e0a9-e50e24dcca9e (read) are preselected if the
+device has them, so Enter on "Connect" is enough.
+.PP
+With ADDRESS, minicom connects to that device directly and skips the
+dialog if both characteristics are found.
+.PP
+Minicom then talks to the device through a pseudo terminal. A small
+helper process relays data between it and the device. Data are written
+in chunks of the ATT MTU, without response if the characteristic allows
+it. If the link drops, a window says so and the helper reconnects by
+itself (also after the adapter has been re-plugged); data typed while
+the link is down are discarded. The device is disconnected when minicom
+exits, unless it was already connected before minicom started. Set
+MINICOM_BLE_LOG to a file name to log what the helper does.
+.RE
+.TP 0.5i
+.B \-\-ble\-adapter=NAME
+Bluetooth adapter to use in BLE serial mode, by name (e.g. hci1) or
+address. Default is the lowest numbered adapter.
+.TP 0.5i
+.B \-\-ble\-write=UUID
+Characteristic to preselect for writing in BLE serial mode.
+.TP 0.5i
+.B \-\-ble\-read=UUID
+Characteristic to preselect for notifications in BLE serial mode.
+.TP 0.5i
 .B \-F, \-\-statlinefmt
 Format for the status line. The following format specifier are available:
    %H  Escape key for help screen.
